SOME SPOILERS FOR NETHACK 2.2a
------------------------------
First, an explanation of some of the syntax used here:
'x/y' means the event occurs x times out of y.
'a..b' means a linear random number is generated from a to b.
=======================
Also used to say that a number which has been determined falls in the
range from a to b inclusive. -PG
=======================
'<a> ? <b> : <c>' means <b> happens if <a> is true, otherwise <c> happens.
'Number from a..b' generates the random number from a to b and then compares
  with the following indented series of numbers to determine what occurs.

